    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-07T16:11:33+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-07T16:11:33+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-07T05:41:33Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-07T05:41:33Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system located near Tasmania maintains a ridge over the state as it moves east into the Tasman Sea. A trough ahead of a strong cold front is expected move over western SA on Thursday, and track east across the rest of SA on Friday. A ridge remains over northern SA on Saturday while a series of troughs and cold fronts move across the state early next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-07T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-07T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Clear. Winds east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds east to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h turning north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h in the late morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 35.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:30am to 4:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers, most likely in the late morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening, possibly severe with damaging winds west of Leigh Creek. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h turning west to northwesterly 35 to 50 km/h in the late morning then tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 28 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Leigh Creek. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers west of Leigh Creek, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
